<title>ITALY: US sees more bumper EU grain crops, poor US wheat.</title>
<headline>US sees more bumper EU grain crops, poor US wheat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior U.S. grain official said on Wednesday that he expected the 1997-98 European Union crop to match last year's high levels, but said the U.S. wheat situation was unlikely to pick up in the year ahead.</p>
<p>However, Lee Schatz, an economist with the U.S. Agriculture Department, told Reuters on the sidelines of an international cereals meeting here that the United States should achieve its export targets this year despite tough competition from southern hemisphere producers.</p>
</text>
